# N0: status of the four-card set, an all-four reset with the heal, then build the tp4-next-2 image (tp4/next-2 = tp4/serve-4, the
# hang-fix arms, merged with tp4/next, the round-time levers) and smoke the PRODUCTION configuration: c2-packed-tp4, the traffic
# profile, audits ON, the tail caps ON, every lever OFF (each tp4/next lever is its own flag and none is in this profile). Run first.
# The build opens no card; the reset first means a card, link or hugepage fault fails here, before the smokes. It runs the image
# copy-closure and overlay tests first and tags the image only if they pass, so a closure error fails here with no card touched.
# The test list is the production smoke of the tp4-serve-6 window (SB, B5), unchanged and in its order: SS, concurrent4_solo, then the
# two coding-text concurrency tests.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image N0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-2 is a PLACEHOLDER: the driver of the window may substitute it (in every template) once the image is built
# from the pushed branch; the driver's IMAGE_TAG env overrides it.
# Duration (estimate, wall clock): status 1-2 min; reset and heal 3-6 min (up to 12); build 7-15 min with the layers cached, 30-70 min
# cold (step limit 75); the smoke 15-25 min. Typical 45 min, at most 120. Check df on the rig first: a new image is about 32 GB.
# Read: the status listing (four boards, one firmware bundle, at least 4 free 1 GiB hugepages, no holders, no platform serving
# container, disk); the build log (closure tests OK, provenance passed, the vglue, fused-commit and lane sources in the image, and the
# [TRIAGE-CHECK] line); then the smoke: '[PINDIAG] packed-any admission passed:' and no UNQUALIFIED line (the reader twin's bytes are
# the evidence's: the vglue attention fold is a subclass in its own module); no late prefill program; c2_smoke_check clean with
# audit_mismatches 0; no lever marker anywhere in the container log (no '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue', no '[PACKED-FUSED]', no '[SOLO-LANE]');
# every concurrent user at 800 tokens; every concurrent4 hash equal to its concurrent4_solo run; speed within 5% of tp4-serve-6's
# production smoke (SB). The production profile must behave as on tp4-serve-6: any difference is the merge's.
# STOP on any failure: a refusal, a hang, or a lever line on the production profile stops the window.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,tool_call,stream_tool_call,stream_reasoning,refused_n2,alive_after_refusal,stream_dropped,alive_after_drop,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal
